      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Two improvements across `parse_dfu_transfer_size()` and `find_dfu_interface()`:\n\n1. **Simplify descriptor traversal with `std::span::subspan()`:** Accepting `std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e extra` allows advancing `extra \u003d extra.subspan(desc_len)` directly instead of maintaining `int off`, `const uint8_t *desc`, and `const uint8_t *sz` pointers, and simplifies the call in `find_dfu_interface()` to `parse_dfu_transfer_size(alt.extra)`.\n2. **Untested / write-only `transfer_size_` member:** `find_dfu_interface()` writes `transfer_size_`, but `RtsUsbDevice` never reads `transfer_size_` (outside `printf`) and exposes no accessor, making the integration of `parse_dfu_transfer_size()` inside `find_dfu_interface()` unverifiable in `RtsUsbDeviceDfuTest`. Please either expose a `uint16_t transfer_size() const { return transfer_size_; }` accessor (and assert on it in `RtsUsbDeviceDfuTest`) or defer `transfer_size_` to the CL that uses it for `DFU_DNLOAD` transfers.\n\n```cpp\nuint16_t parse_dfu_transfer_size(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e extra)\n{\n\t/*\n\t * Walk the descriptor stream.  The DFU functional descriptor has type\n\t * 0x21 and contains wTransferSize at byte offset 5-6.\n\t */\n\twhile (extra.size() \u003e kDfuDescTypeOff) {\n\t\tuint8_t desc_len \u003d extra[0];\n\n\t\tif (desc_len \u003d\u003d 0 || desc_len \u003e extra.size())\n\t\t\tbreak;\n\n\t\tif (extra[kDfuDescTypeOff] \u003d\u003d kDfuDescriptorType \u0026\u0026\n\t\t    desc_len \u003e\u003d kDfuDescMinLen) {\n\t\t\tuint16_t size \u003d extra[kDfuDescXferSizeOff] |\n\t\t\t\t\t(extra[kDfuDescXferSizeOff + 1] \u003c\u003c 8);\n\n\t\t\treturn size !\u003d 0 ? size : kDfuDefaultTransferSize;\n\t\t}\n\t\textra \u003d extra.subspan(desc_len);\n\t}\n\n\treturn kDfuDefaultTransferSize;\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/133da944-0407-4c57-82eb-1e99128ae54b)",
