      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Please address the following test coverage and readability items in the new test suites:\n\n1. **Missing boundary cases in `ParseDfuTransferSizeTest`:**\n   * **Exact 1-byte buffer boundary (`extra.size() \u003d\u003d kDfuDescTypeOff`):** `NullOrEmptyUsesDefault` tests length `0`, and other tests use `\u003e\u003d 3` bytes, leaving the exact loop-condition boundary `extra.size() \u003d\u003d kDfuDescTypeOff` (`1` byte, e.g. `{ 0x01 }`) untested. Testing a 1-byte buffer ensures `extra[kDfuDescTypeOff]` is not read out of bounds if `\u003c` were accidentally written as `\u003c\u003d`.\n   * **Descriptor longer than `kDfuDescMinLen` (`desc_len \u003d\u003d kDfuDescMinLen + 1`):** `desc_len \u003e\u003d kDfuDescMinLen` is tested at `kDfuDescMinLen - 1` and `kDfuDescMinLen`, but never at `kDfuDescMinLen + 1` (e.g. an extended DFU descriptor with trailing byte).\n2. **Verify `transfer_size` parsing in `RtsUsbDeviceDfuTest`:** In `DetachSendsRequestToDfuInterface`, pass a non-default transfer size (e.g. `dfu_interface(2, 2048)`) and assert `EXPECT_EQ(device_-\u003etransfer_size(), 2048);` so that `find_dfu_interface()`\u0027s call to `parse_dfu_transfer_size()` is verified.\n3. **Avoid magic numbers and multi-line field-by-field struct initialization in tests:**\n   * Replace magic literals (`9` on line 234, `0x03`/`0x01` on lines 347-348, and unexplained descriptor bytes in `dfu_func_desc`) with named constants or inline field comments.\n   * Use designated initializers when constructing `RtsUsbInterface` in `dfu_interface()`, `DetachFailsWithoutDfuInterface`, and `DetachSendsRequestToDfuInterface`:\n\n```cpp\nTEST(ParseDfuTransferSizeTest, SingleByteBufferUsesDefault)\n{\n\tconst std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e extra \u003d { 0x01 };\n\n\tEXPECT_EQ(parse_dfu_transfer_size(extra), kDfuDefaultTransferSize);\n}\n\nTEST(ParseDfuTransferSizeTest, ValidDescriptorLongerThanMinLength)\n{\n\tauto extra \u003d dfu_func_desc(2048);\n\n\textra[0] \u003d kDfuDescMinLen + 1;\n\textra.push_back(0x00);\n\tEXPECT_EQ(parse_dfu_transfer_size(extra), 2048);\n}\n```\n\nAnd in `RtsUsbDeviceDfuTest`:\n\n```cpp\n\tRtsUsbInterface dfu_interface(int number, uint16_t transfer_size)\n\t{\n\t\treturn {\n\t\t\t.number \u003d number,\n\t\t\t.usb_class \u003d kDfuClass,\n\t\t\t.usb_subclass \u003d kDfuSubclass,\n\t\t\t.extra \u003d dfu_func_desc(transfer_size),\n\t\t};\n\t}\n...\nTEST_F(RtsUsbDeviceDfuTest, DetachFailsWithoutDfuInterface)\n{\n\tconstexpr uint8_t kHidClass \u003d 0x03;\n\n\texpect_interfaces({\n\t\tRtsUsbInterface{\n\t\t\t.number \u003d 0,\n\t\t\t.usb_class \u003d kHidClass,\n\t\t\t.usb_subclass \u003d kDfuSubclass,\n\t\t},\n\t});\n\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, control_transfer(_, _, _, _, _, _, _)).Times(0);\n\n\tEXPECT_FALSE(device_-\u003edfu_detach(1000));\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/133da944-0407-4c57-82eb-1e99128ae54b)",
